pleted":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in v4.5.beta5.official [c81fd6c51] and v4.4.1.stable.official [49a5bc7b6]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.beta5 - Windows 11 (build 22631) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4090 Laptop GPU (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7688) - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-13900HX (32 threads) - 63.74 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen the SpriteFrames panel for AnimatedSprite2D is in focus, the shortcut keys described in the icons don't function at all.\n\nAll of these commands only work for me if I click the buttons manually.\n\nSo hitting A, SHIFT + A, S, SHIFT + D, and D doesn't process any of those things. I have to manually click the buttons. Tried it on 4.4.1 and 4.5 and had the same problem.\n\nI also checked the command palette and there are no shortcuts to bind in there.\n\nHitting CTRL + N, WILL make a new animation properly. \n\n<img width=\"1777\" height=\"1645\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9f425f60-0346-4508-a0fe-69f54a161486\" />\n\n<img width=\"2875\" height=\"586\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/adc9b6ab-be48-48fe-9091-388be62f023b\" />\n\n### Expected Behavior\n\nI expect that pressing D on the keyboard will cause the animation to start playing from the current position, ect.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Select the AnimatedSprite2D Node under the Player node in the Player scene.\n2. click into the Animation player\n3. Press any of the shortcut keys (A, SHIFT + A, S, SHIFT + D, and D)\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[SpriteFrames Bug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/21674887/SpriteFrames.Bug.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_